WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:06.140
Emilio Estevez was once listed among Hollywood's
most popular actors.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:11.440
Born into a screen-savvy family that included
Martin and Charlie Sheen and raised among

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.870
other rising stars, Estevez was part of the
"Brat Pack," a young crowd of A-list actors

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:21.519
that graced the screen in a string of hit
films during the '80s and early '90s.

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:26.960
In recent years, however, Estevez has seemingly
slipped off the pop culture radar.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.289
Here's how it happened.

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:30.509
The Outsider

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:34.840
Estevez starred in some of the most beloved
flicks of the mid-'80s, and even though the

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:40.370
popularity of those pics has lasted for generations,
he's been resistant to rejoining his former

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:45.820
castmates for the celebratory cast reunions
that have taken place over the years.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.550
According to fellow Breakfast Club alum Molly
Ringwald, he's the only one who doesn't keep

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.030
in touch with the others, even when there
aren't any cameras around.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.190
She told Australia's The Morning Show:

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.899
"The only person I don't really see is Emilio
Estevez.

00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:03.350
He really won't have anything to do with anything
having to do with this movie…

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.110
He's just like, 'That's the past, and that's
not really what I want to do.'"

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:11.580
As for why he refuses to get nostalgic with
the rest of the pack, it's hard to say.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:16.540
He's certainly shown some social media support
for another fan favorite, The Mighty Ducks,

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:21.510
by live-tweeting a crucial match-up involving
the Anaheim Ducks with some familiar "quack,

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.050
quack" terminology.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:25.370
"We're the Ducks!"

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.690
"The Mighty Ducks!"

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:30.090
Man at Work

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.560
Like a lot of Hollywood stars, Estevez has
invested in side businesses to keep himself

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.990
busy when he's not working on films.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:43.300
In his case, he quietly owned a vineyard in
Malibu making Pinot Noir and other vintages

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.470
for several years with his former fiancée,
Sonja Magdevski.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:52.430
As he told The Hollywood Reporter, he and
Magdevski initially bonded over making wine

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:53.430
together.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:54.430
He explained:

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:57.620
"On our first date, I dug the holes and she
planted the vines.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:01.460
There was never any grandiose plan to start
a winery."

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:08.140
Things escalated from there, and they established
Casa Dumetz Wines in 2004, complete with a

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.420
Los Alamos tasting room and appearances at
high-profile food and wine festivals.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.750
The couple ran the business for over a decade
before their split, and he eventually sold

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.210
the vineyard in 2016.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.210
The Wars at Home

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:22.910
There's no doubt that Charlie Sheen has emerged
as the more well-known of the Sheen/Estevez

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:26.640
children, but these days he's more infamous
than famous.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:32.010
Sheen has very publicly struggled with issues
of addiction, relationship woes, and financial

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:37.850
crises, and Estevez has said that he believes
his duty is to provide a healthy lifestyle

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.500
example for his problem-plagued sibling.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.390
He told The Sunday Times in 2011:

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:48.120
"All I can do for Charlie, and I can't live
his life for him, is to try to be an example.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.290
But really, I was a pretty poor one.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:56.400
As a kid, I was smart enough to be surreptitious
about all my misbehavior, or at least stealthy.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.900
But it means that my opinions carry little
weight with Charlie."

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:03.480
That's not the only crisis Emilio's been dealing
with on the homefront.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:09.350
In an open letter to fans of his film The
Way in 2015, Estevez revealed that he and

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:14.380
his family had banded together to support
his father Martin Sheen through the quadruple

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.230
bypass surgery to repair his heart.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:22.550
That was only a month after Charlie Sheen
revealed that he had been diagnosed with HIV,

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:27.180
and according to Martin Sheen, the family
came together to support the actor's decision

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.230
to reveal his struggle with the disease.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.550
The Mighty Duck

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:35.760
Although both Charlie and Martin Sheen got
their second career winds on the small screen

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.590
— starring in The West Wing and Two and
a Half Men, respectively — Estevez has shied

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:45.800
away from television, even at a time when
it's arguably at a golden era for actors of

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:46.880
his ilk.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:52.410
Estevez did come in for single-episode guest
stints on each of those series, but most of

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:58.340
his TV-related work has been behind the lens,
directing several episodes of shows like CSI:

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.959
NY and Numbers.

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:02.190
The New Way

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:07.580
Estevez has also written and directed several
of his own feature films, including the 1990

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:12.730
action-comedy caper pic Men at Work, which
featured himself alongside his brother.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:18.959
His crowning achievement came in 2006 with
his Golden Globe-nominated historical biopic

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:24.630
Bobby, about the assassination of Senator
Robert F. Kennedy — an event which Estevez

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:28.419
considered to be of grave importance to American
history.

00:04:28.419 --> 00:04:33.639
His most recent effort, the aforementioned
The Way from 2010, featured Estevez alongside

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:39.080
his father, who starred as a grieving parent
on a spiritual adventure in France while retrieving

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.580
his son's ashes.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:45.800
He's also been working to make Cincinnati,
Ohio a new hotspot for Hollywood movies.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:51.639
In 2016, Estevez made a rare appearance at
the Sundance Film Festival to speak to members

00:04:51.639 --> 00:04:56.160
of the Cincinnati Film Commission about his
hopes to bolster the city's film industry

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:01.580
opportunities as a nod to his father's upbringing
in nearby Dayton, Ohio.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:06.999
Estevez himself has put his money where his
mouth is on this issue, as he shot his as-yet-unreleased

00:05:06.999 --> 00:05:09.689
pic Johnny Longshot in the city.

00:05:09.689 --> 00:05:10.860
Stakeout

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:16.259
Estevez has found his name and face on the
cover of many a tabloid over the years, particularly

00:05:16.259 --> 00:05:22.009
when it came to the dissolutions of his relationships
with ex-fiancée Demi Moore and his former

00:05:22.009 --> 00:05:24.770
wife, pop starlet Paula Abdul.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:28.940
Considering the crowd he kept company with
— and the wild antics of his brother, no

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:34.029
doubt — Estevez said he faced allegations
in the court of public opinion that he was

00:05:34.029 --> 00:05:37.779
a "partier and a womanizer," but that it just
wasn't true.

00:05:37.779 --> 00:05:42.069
After suffering the spotlight, Estevez has
lost interest in maintaining his celebrity

00:05:42.069 --> 00:05:45.819
— or even knowing who the paparazzi are
following now.

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:50.749
Even so, he's admitted to looking himself
up online and regretting it almost instantly.

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:51.800
As he told The Guardian:

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:56.340
"When journalists think that actors don't
read what is written about them, they are

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:57.340
mistaken.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:02.589
I would put my name in a Google site and see
what came up and often it was very hurtful.

00:06:02.589 --> 00:06:04.400
Hollywood is guilty of turning out s***.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:09.589
I've turned it out myself, but what the journalists
don't do is to take a moment to think that

00:06:09.589 --> 00:06:13.559
maybe this actor has got a family and he has
got to feed them."

00:06:13.559 --> 00:06:16.090
No wonder he's been so shy lately …

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:17.090
Thanks for watching!

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.999
